<title>CANADA: Philip sees higher revenues from deals.</title>
<headline>Philip sees higher revenues from deals.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philip Environmental Inc said on Wednesday that three recent acquisitions will add about US$430 million in annual revenue and boost the company's earnings.</p>
<p>Philip said in a statement that it has closed the acquisitions of Ohio-based Luntz Corp, Intsel Southwest Partnership of Texas, and the Alcan Alloys plant in Guelph, Ontario.</p>
<p>&quot;These transactions wil contribute approximately US$430 million in annual revenue and have an accretive impact on Philip's earnings per share,&quot; the company said.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100))</p>
</text>
